@ 37.2.6.3 - Proto-Dhegiha to Osage
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Wolff, Hans (1950), “Comparative Siouan I”. International Journal of American Linguistics 16(2):61 – 66; Wolff, Hans (1950), “Comparative Siouan II” International Journal of American Linguistics 16(3):113 – 121; Wolff, Hans (1950), “Comparative Siouan III”. International Journal of American Linguistics 16(4):168 – 178; and cedh audmanh’s changes above, which assisted me in deciphering the vintage phonetic transcription scheme NB: Does not include developments in unstressed non-nasal vowels. L was apparently either /ɹ/ or /l/; Lʲ (Lʸ in the text) was apparently /j/, or maybe /ʎ/.
	p > p, b, m, w / _C
	t > t͡s / _:[+front]
	s > θ
	{ç,x} > z (sporadic)
	n > ð / :{ _ã, _ẽ, _õ }:
	w > b / #_
	Lʲ > ð / _V:[+nas -stress]
	ʔ > ∅ / p_
	t > t͡s / _ʔ
	{ pr, sr, tʲr, kr } > { bð, st͡s, ʃd, ɡð }
	r > ð / x_
	m > ∅ / #_n
	mn > bð / :{ {C,V}_C, {C,V}_V }:
	{ sn, mt } > { hn, d }
	ʃ > s / V_k
	xk > (ʃ)k / _V
	xk > ɡ / V_
	x > ʔ / k_V